Before submitting an exception, review our Exception Management Process on ANCHOR. 

# [EXCEPTION] <short descriptive title>
One or two lines: what this is, the parent issue, and any associated PRs.

## Risk Level
Low, Medium, or High as assessed by our Risk Assessment Matrix on ANCHOR.

## Business Justification
The problem this solves and why it needs to be done.

## Length of Exception
The expected length this exception needs to be in place; if longer than one year, annual re-submission and re-approval will be required.

## Compensating Controls
What controls were put in place to ensure the exception does not introduce risk.

## Communication Plan
Who needs to be informed, and any written comms plans. If none, use N/A.
